    "summary": "Carved wooden spoon with ovoid bowl bi-sected into two halves by a longitudinal black painted line on the inner surface.  The spoon has a long tapered handle with a notched stem.  The terminal of the handle has a small rectangular slot cut into the middle of it.  The terminal and the lower end of the neck are also painted black. There are two small chips on the rim of the spoon bowl on one side.",
